  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Figs 26 and 27, current-state (March 2024) and future-state supply chain systems in Ethiopia. Current state: an OpenHIM interoperability layer, a master health facility registry, a national product catalogue under development and terminology services, DHIS2 and EMR, and supply chain systems including VITAS, FANOS, DAGU, eLMIS, eAPTs and eRIS, with eTrade and eCustom as external systems; a legend colours each by its state. Future state: the layered architecture with an ERP at national level, DAGU, eAPTs and mBrana at facility level, a product directory service, track and trace and product verification, and GFPVAN, manufacturers, eTrade and eCustom as external systems.",
      "lang": "en",
